<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Applying the addition and complement rules to quality control defects</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A manufacturing plant in Athi River produces digital tablets. Quality control records show that for any randomly selected tablet:</p>
<ul>
  <li>The probability it has a cosmetic defect (Event \(C\)) is \(P(C) = {@str_C@}\).</li>
  <li>The probability it has a functional defect (Event \(F\)) is \(P(F) = {@str_F@}\).</li>
  <li>The probability it has <b>both</b> a cosmetic and a functional defect is \(P(C \cap F) = {@str_both@}\).</li>
</ul>

<p><b>a) </b> Find the probability that a tablet has <b>at least one</b> defect (either cosmetic, functional, or both).</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as an exact decimal).</i></p>
<p>\(P(C \cup F) =\) [[input:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><b>b) </b> Find the probability that a tablet has <b>neither</b> defect (it is in perfect condition).</p>
<p>\(P((C \cup F)') =\) [[input:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part a: At Least One Defect</b><br>
The probability of at least one defect is the union of the two events. We use the general addition rule:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(C \cup F) = P(C) + P(F) - P(C \cap F) \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(C \cup F) = {@str_C@} + {@str_F@} - {@str_both@} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P(C \cup F) = {@ta1_str@} } \)</p>

<p><b>Part b: No Defects</b><br>
Having "neither defect" is the exact complement of having "at least one defect". We use the complement rule:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P((C \cup F)') = 1 - P(C \cup F) \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P((C \cup F)') = 1 - {@ta1_str@} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P((C \cup F)') = {@ta2_str@} } \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
